topic "Mobile And Tablet"
    description "Touchscreen controls for Minecraft Bedrock Edition on phones and tablets."

    section "Movement"
        subsection "Touch Movement"
            text
Use the on-screen movement controls to move your character.

Depending on your selected touch control scheme, movement controls may appear in different locations.
            end
        end

        subsection "Jumping"
            text
Use the on-screen jump button to jump.

When flying in Creative Mode, use the on-screen controls to move vertically.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Looking Around"
        subsection "Camera"
            text
Drag across the screen to look around.

The exact camera behavior depends on the selected touch-control configuration.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Actions"
        subsection "Breaking Blocks"
            text
Press and hold a block to break it.

The amount of time required depends on the block and the item being used.
            end
        end

        subsection "Placing And Interacting"
            text
Tap the screen to place a block or interact with an available object, depending on the current control layout.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Hotbar"
        subsection "Selecting Items"
            text
Tap an item in the hotbar to select it.

Swipe across the hotbar when supported to change the selected item.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Inventory And Items"
        subsection "Inventory"
            text
Tap the inventory button to open the inventory.

Touch controls for moving, splitting, and combining item stacks are displayed within the inventory interface.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Chat And Commands"
        subsection "Chat"
            text
Use the chat button to open the chat interface.

Use the on-screen keyboard to enter messages and commands.
            end
        end

        subsection "Commands"
            text
Type / at the beginning of a message to enter a command.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Creative Mode"
        subsection "Creative Inventory"
            text
Open the Creative inventory to browse blocks and items.

Tap an item to select it.
            end
        end

        subsection "Flying"
            text
Use the touchscreen flight controls when flying in Creative Mode.

The exact controls depend on the selected touch-control layout.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Touch Control Settings"
        subsection "Changing Touch Controls"
            text
Open Settings and select Touch to view available touchscreen control options.

Minecraft Bedrock Edition provides different touchscreen control schemes and options depending on the version and device.
            end
        end
    end
end

topic "Changing Controls"
    description "How to customize controls in Minecraft Bedrock Edition."

    section "Keyboard And Mouse"
        subsection "Opening Settings"
            text
Open the Minecraft Settings menu.

Select Keyboard & Mouse to view the available keyboard and mouse bindings.
            end
        end

        subsection "Changing A Binding"
            text
Select the action you want to change.

Choose its current key binding and press the new key or mouse button you want to assign.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Controller"
        subsection "Opening Controller Settings"
            text
Open the Minecraft Settings menu.

Select Controller to view the available controller controls and customization options.
            end
        end

        subsection "Changing A Binding"
            text
Select an available control and assign the button or input you want to use when the option is supported.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Touch"
        subsection "Opening Touch Settings"
            text
Open the Minecraft Settings menu.

Select Touch to view touchscreen control options.
            end
        end

        subsection "Changing The Touch Layout"
            text
Choose from the available touch-control schemes and configure the options provided by your version of Minecraft Bedrock Edition.
            end
        end
    end

    section "Resetting Controls"
        subsection "Reset To Defaults"
            warning
Resetting controls returns customized bindings to their default settings. Make sure you want to remove your custom bindings before confirming the reset.
            end
        end
    end
end

topic "Control Categories"
    description "A reference for the major types of controls used throughout Minecraft Bedrock Edition."

    section "Movement"
        text
Movement controls change your character's position in the world, including walking, sprinting, sneaking, jumping, swimming, and flying.
        end
    end

    section "Camera"
        text
Camera controls change the direction you are looking.
        end
    end

    section "Interaction"
        text
Interaction controls are used for placing blocks, using items, opening containers, activating objects, and interacting with entities.
        end
    end

    section "Combat"
        text
Combat controls are used to attack entities and defend yourself.
        end
    end

    section "Inventory"
        text
Inventory controls are used to manage items, equipment, crafting materials, and containers.
        end
    end

    section "Interface"
        text
Interface controls are used to open menus, chat, settings, inventories, and other game screens.
        end
    end

    section "Creative"
        text
Creative controls include flying, accessing the Creative inventory, and quickly selecting blocks and items.
        end
    end
end

topic "Important Notes"
    description "Important information about Minecraft Bedrock Edition controls."

    section "Control Differences"
        text
Controls can differ between keyboard and mouse, Xbox, PlayStation, Nintendo Switch, mobile, and tablet devices.

Some controls may also change between Minecraft Bedrock Edition versions.
        end
    end

    section "Custom Bindings"
        text
If you change a control in Settings, the customized binding takes precedence over the default binding shown in this document.
        end
    end

    section "Control Schemes"
        text
Touchscreen devices may provide multiple control schemes. The controls displayed on screen depend on the selected scheme and device.
        end
    end

    section "Version Changes"
        note
Minecraft Bedrock Edition receives updates that can change controls, menus, and available settings. If a control does not match your game, check the current Settings menu for the binding assigned to that action.
        end
    end
end